WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.080
So recently I had a client of mine
ringing me up

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:06.160
and she was in a really
tricky situation.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:10.200
Her and her boyfriend of three years
have basically just broken up.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.840
Now, they live
in the same flat together

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:16.000
and they've got five months
left on the contract.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.520
So not only are they going
to have to share the flat

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.560
for another five months,
but because it's a one bed flat,

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.120
they're going to have to share
the same bed.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.120
Can you even imagine
how difficult that must be?

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:31.360
I remember helping one couple
in particular whose communication

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:35.720
had become so toxic, that they could
no longer hear and understand

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.200
what the other was asking.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.040
All they heard were
their worst fears.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.520
Let's face it,
breaking up is never easy.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.800
But when you're in a situation that
forces you to get on with an ex,

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:49.080
it can be a really difficult
divide to cross.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:02.160
People fall madly in love
and in my experience,

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:04.720
they fall madly out of love as well.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.880
You might find yourself
in a tricky situation

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:10.000
if you live in the same halls
as your ex at university

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:13.320
or you go to a party
or a wedding of a mutual friend

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.680
or you happen to work together.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.680
Often the people I help
share children and assets.

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:22.080
And although you may not
like them at the moment,

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:26.200
your ex is likely to be
your best possible resource

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:28.720
to help you look after your children

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.800
and create the life
that you want for yourself.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:35.760
A messy breakup means that
you need to find creative ways

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:36.920
to cross the divide.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.240
I know it's not always possible

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:47.080
but really try to give one another
proper space after the breakup.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:51.480
Ideally commit to going around six
months to one year of no contact,

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:54.080
just so that you give yourselves
the chance to get each other

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:55.360
out of your systems.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.360
Take advice from all sources -

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:05.520
Accountants, tax advisors,
benefit officers -

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.840
whatever is going
to help you the most.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:11.080
If you have an area
that you're afraid of,

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:14.000
if you're afraid of finances...
get help.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:18.120
Don’t ignore it or stick your head in
the sand and hope it will go away,

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.320
it won't.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.880
Embrace it and grow.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:28.680
When you do see your ex
in a social situation,

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:33.520
go out of your way to take the high
road, however difficult that may be.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:36.160
Say hello, be graceful, be mature.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.280
So I was in a situation like this
myself a few years ago.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:42.280
I had been asked to do
a speech at a festival

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:45.560
about a book that I'd written,
now this book was mainly

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:48.520
about a really painful breakup
that I'd had with an ex.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:52.440
And my new boyfriend of a year
had come to watch me do this talk.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.280
And as the workshop started,

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:59.280
in walks my ex, from the book,
with his new girlfriend.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.960
And look, this could have been
such an awkward situation

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:04.560
for my new boyfriend, but as soon
as the workshop was over,

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:07.480
he went right up to my ex,
introduced himself

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.600
and they ended up really,
really getting on.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:13.640
So much so, that he
has very recently asked my ex

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:16.720
to be an usher at our
wedding next year.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:25.880
Get in touch with the new you
and who you want to be.

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:28.880
Think about where you might
want to be in a year's time.

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:34.480
Be curious about those options,
think about your wider context.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:37.720
Get back in touch with your passions,
your friends

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.960
and the person that you may have
compromised in the relationship.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:44.400
Focus on the future and the person
you want to be,

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:47.240
rather than the painful events
that may have taken place.

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.640
Whatever you do,
do not put your mutual friends

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:59.440
in an awkward position by making
them choose between you and your ex

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:02.440
or talking really negatively about
your ex behind their back.

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:05.400
Trust me, this does not
put you in a good light.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:15.240
Mentalise and empathise
with your ex-partner's needs

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:16.760
and try to be objective.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:20.280
It takes a great deal
of emotional effort

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.120
to see your ex through that lens.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.240
But remember you did love them once,

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:27.000
and you did see their
positive attributes.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:29.920
They still have them,
you just can't see them right now.

